{"results": [{"article_id": "KB-429", "title": "Statutes of limitations", "last_reviewed": "2026-06-06", "audience": "clients", "body": "Every claim has a legal deadline, called a statute of limitations, which varies by claim type and state. Claims against government entities often require a written notice within six months.

Missing a deadline can bar a claim entirely. An estimated date can come from the firm's deadline calculator, but only an attorney can confirm it.

Deadlines are calendared by the paralegal team at intake and reviewed by the assigned attorney.", "related": ["Typical case timelines", "Confidentiality and privacy"]}]}

